      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T06:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Defaulting to 0 changes the effective default. Previously acceptorThreads (2) was mis-passed as the selector count, so runtime topology was 0 acceptors / 2 selectors. Now acceptors\u003d2, and with a SizedThreadPool at the default maxThreads\u003d25 the derived selector count is 1 — i.e. 2 acceptors / 1 selector.\n\nIs 2 acceptors / 1 selector the intended new default, or should we preserve the historical 0 / 2 (acceptorThreads\u003d0, selectorThreads\u003d2)? Either way the shift is worth calling out — which the commit-message and release-note comments now do.",
